------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Presentations of groups
--
-- On three wires, the circuit presentation (Circuits.Syntactics) and
-- the paper's with the definition of K (Repaired.Syntactics) present
-- the same group
--
-- ι reads a circuit letter as the paper's letter for that gate on
-- those qubits (H on wire 1 and 2 as the paper's words H₁, H₀), and κ
-- reads a paper letter as the circuit of the same name.  A circuit
-- rule is a paper rule read through κ, so it holds in the paper's
-- presentation once each letter is its reading back (ικ: Figure 4's
-- definitions); a paper rule is a circuit rule, a definition, or a
-- structural commutation; and κ ∘ ι is the identity but for H.  The
-- commutations of gates on disjoint wires that the paper does not
-- state are derived through its completeness (Repaired.Presentation),
-- the two sides having the same matrix.  So (ι ʷ) is a group
-- isomorphism of the presented groups.
--
-- Generated by tools/gen_circuits.py from Syntactics.
------------------------------------------------------------------------

